<title>RUSSIA: Russia sows more food grain, less maize, beets.</title>
<headline>Russia sows more food grain, less maize, beets.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russia's spring sowing campaign is nearly over, with wheat sowings up five percent but maize (corn) and sugar beet plantings far below year-ago levels, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>Maize sowings were 18 percent below 1996's level, while sugar beet plantings were 20 percent down year-on year.</p>
<p>The total area sown thus far to winter and spring grains, to be harvested this fall, was 46.1 million hectares, or eight percent below year-ago levels, the committee said.</p>
